      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers, or make your own offer - Register now at SherryFitz.ie\n\nThe property has been vacant for over 2 years and may be eligible for the Vacant Homes Grant.\n\nNestled amidst the peaceful countryside of Ballynashee, Geevagh this beautifully restored early 1900s residence offers a rare opportunity to enjoy idyllic rural living in one of County Sligo's most scenic locations on a circa 2.19 acre site.\n\nCombining the charm and character of a traditional Irish farmhouse with thoughtful modern upgrades and an extension completed over the years, this delightful four-bedroom home is surrounded by mature trees, natural beauty, and complete privacy.\n\nA gentle stream meanders along the property's boundary, creating a wonderfully tranquil backdrop, while the abundance of mature planting enhances the sense of seclusion. Whether you're seeking a permanent family home, a peaceful retreat, or a charming country residence with character, this property would be ideal for you.\n\nInternally, the home is filled with warmth and personality. Original features such as exposed ceiling beams and impressive feature fireplaces blend effortlessly with practical modern comforts. \n\nThe property benefits from a number of valuable recent improvements including a roof replaced approximately 12 years ago and a new septic tank installed approximately one year ago. A private water well is conveniently located to the rear of the property. Internet is was previously provided via a 4G modem.\n\nSituated in the heart of the beautiful Sligo countryside, Ballynashee offers exceptional peace and privacy while remaining accessible to nearby towns and everyday amenities.\n\nGeevagh village is only a brief drive away and provides local conveniences including a primary school, community centre and sporting facilities. The larger towns of Boyle and Carrick-on-Shannon are both within easy reach.\n\nThe surrounding area is renowned for its natural beauty with numerous scenic walks, forest trails and outdoor pursuits nearby. Lough Arrow, Lough Key Forest Park and the Bricklieve Mountains are all within comfortable driving distance, making this an ideal base for those who appreciate the outdoors.\n\nGeevagh - 5 minutesBoyle - 20 minutes Carrick-on-Shannon - 25 minutes Sligo - 35 minutes"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - 1.52m x 1.25m\nGlazed entrance door, floor tiling.\n\nLiving Room - 4.32m x 4.29m\nFormerly a kitchen area with floor tiling, feature fireplace with De Dietrich range, storage space, curtain pole x 3, ceiling beams.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - 5.15m x 4.98m\nFloor tiling, fitted kitchen units, electric oven, gas hob, extractor fan, curtain pole & drapes, recessed down lights, wall light, external side door, radiator.\n\nSitting Room - 5.91m x 4.52m\nSpacious, dual aspect room.Wood flooring, feature fireplace, ceiling beams, radiator x 2, feature wall lamps x 4.\n\nBack Porch - 2.88m x 1.67m\nInc. Guest WCFloor tiling, external entrance door, shelving, window blind x 2, wc&whb.\n\nFirst Floor - 7.79m x 1.98m\nCarpet, airing cupboard, radiator.\n\nMaster Bedroom - 5.21m x 5.01m\nInc. En-SuiteWood flooring, radiator, curtain pole & drapes.En-suite - tiled, jacuzzi bath with mixer taps, extractor fan, radiator, under sink cabinet.\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.58m x 3.03m\nPleasant, dual aspect room, with raised ceiling, wood flooring, ceiling beams, curtain poles x 3, radiator.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.63m x 2.57m\nWood flooring, ceiling beams, radiator.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.52m x 2.55m\nWood flooring, ceiling beams, curtain pole, radiator.\n\nBathroom - \n\n\nBathroom - 2.69m x 1.63m\nStain glass window, tiled, shower enclosure with electric shower, wc&whb, extractor home, Creda wall heater, radiator, recessed down lights.\n\nExternal - \nLovely, elevated site on circa 2.19 acres of groundsOil condenser burner, oil tankWater wellNew septic tank - circa 1 year old\n\n - \nThese particulars have been prepared by Sherry FitzGerald Farrell and whilst every care has been taken to ensure that these are accurate and correct, we are not responsible for any errors, omissions, inaccuracies, if the property is let, sold or withdrawn from sale or if it is not suitable for your purpose. These particulars are for information only and are given under the strict understanding that they do not form part of any contract. Neither whole nor any part of this document or any reference thereto may be included in any public document, circular or statement nor published without the written consent of Sherry FitzGerald Farrell.\n\n"
